                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9b29aaf2-3576-4a1e-b6e6-bca458815188",
                                "sense_id": "7c236d1c-0ce7-352b-8aac-beb738b7d7cc",
                                "text": "Teraz szli w jak najlepszej zgodzie ze swymi odwiecznymi wrogami, dzielili się z nimi betelem, powszechnie tu uznawanym za symbol pokoju."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "63e5c18f-50dc-4515-8625-3902f1a3a1e3",
                        "source_entry_id": "0278e90f-1354-348c-a5fb-ef51bd41244e",
                        "source_sense_id": "7c236d1c-0ce7-352b-8aac-beb738b7d7cc",
                        "target_lang_word": "immemorial",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "immemorial",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e2b3a84a-8cab-37aa-bf88-077fb4ce3caf",
                                        "entry_id": "15e1a111-5e22-3d4f-b319-c4b709fe1d95",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "That is beyond memory; ancient."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "postpositional",
                                            "sometimes"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "282ed474-95e4-4fec-8bdc-ed239b56d3f8",
                                                "sense_id": "e2b3a84a-8cab-37aa-bf88-077fb4ce3caf",
                                                "text": "The rocks had stood overlooking the valley since time immemorial."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b0ca676a-37ce-42e6-9b08-6e52ff2d114f",
                                                "sense_id": "e2b3a84a-8cab-37aa-bf88-077fb4ce3caf",
                                                "text": "We will ride this morning to what we call the grove of Daphne. It is a real laurel grove. Some of the trees must be immemorial, and deserve to have been sacred, if once they were not so."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dd540cee-2bef-43e0-9575-95818d135ed1",
                                                "sense_id": "e2b3a84a-8cab-37aa-bf88-077fb4ce3caf",
                                                "text": "...the fact of the immemorial taking of the toll, though it would be rightful in its origin if the spot was in a port, and wrongful if it was not in a port, did not of itself afford sufficient ground for inferring that the spot was an antient port, or that such special services were rendered, either by express stipulation in some lost grant, or by immemorial usage, as would support such a grant or custom."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2e1fbdf0-082a-4255-9cfb-9bd3540b51df",
                                                "sense_id": "e2b3a84a-8cab-37aa-bf88-077fb4ce3caf",
                                                "text": "Now, I still think that for this box of matches to have escaped the wear of time for immemorial years was a strange, and for me, a most fortunate thing."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6f665308-c544-466b-b97f-eb38f683b387",
                        "source_entry_id": "0278e90f-1354-348c-a5fb-ef51bd41244e",
                        "source_sense_id": "7c236d1c-0ce7-352b-8aac-beb738b7d7cc",
                        "target_lang_word": "long-time",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "long-time",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0a6ab555-2837-33c5-a751-2e2af8f305b0",
                                        "entry_id": "67e23453-3670-344f-a56b-1c2d33e64953",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative spelling of longtime."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f9ac411-372f-4481-b8eb-f38c75e563e9",
                                                "sense_id": "0a6ab555-2837-33c5-a751-2e2af8f305b0",
                                                "text": "Wellings has form here, having in 2015 written a pamphlet with long-time anti-rail campaigner Paul Withrington entitled Paving over the Tracks: a Better Use of Britain's Railways."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "18246cbe-9a85-4b2e-9582-9a49e736405e",
                        "source_entry_id": "0278e90f-1354-348c-a5fb-ef51bd41244e",
                        "source_sense_id": "7c236d1c-0ce7-352b-8aac-beb738b7d7cc",
                        "target_lang_word": "age-old",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "age-old",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "be376e31-4daf-3606-843f-517c3bea4923",
                                        "entry_id": "d21052b7-d79b-3dfb-af41-4f439fb89b33",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Very old; having existed for a long time; ancient or well-established."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0a1500b7-cbf1-4afb-be43-608df2eeb055",
                                                "sense_id": "be376e31-4daf-3606-843f-517c3bea4923",
                                                "text": "They still make pottery by hand, in the age-old tradition."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "271e60f8-f5e5-4091-a7c1-ee956a81a5ca",
                                                "sense_id": "be376e31-4daf-3606-843f-517c3bea4923",
                                                "text": "It is a striking fact that it seems to be an age-old tradition amongst locomotive designers that a 0-6-0 tender engine must have inside cylinders."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d8a052e5-58cc-4a43-93ea-e7f50fbe6ef7",
                                                "sense_id": "be376e31-4daf-3606-843f-517c3bea4923",
                                                "text": "And on a programme of works of this magnitude, passengers will need to be mindful of the age-old maxim of 'no gain without pain'."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
